---
import SectionLabel from "./SectionLabel.astro";

const faqs = [
  ["How much does a project cost?", "It depends on scope, timeline, and complexity. A website or portal is usually smaller than an MVP or product rescue. The first call is used to understand the work and suggest the right engagement."],
  ["How long does a website or portal take?", "Timelines depend on content, integrations, workflows, and review speed. Smaller websites or portals can move quickly, while more involved systems are scoped after discovery."],
  ["How long does an MVP take?", "MVP timelines depend on features, integrations, and quality expectations. CodeVault starts by defining the smallest useful version that can be launched and tested."],
  ["Can you work with my existing codebase?", "Yes. For existing projects, the first step is usually an audit to understand the structure, bugs, risks, and best path forward."],
  ["Can you design and build?", "Yes. CodeVault can handle structure, UI direction, frontend, backend, integrations, and deployment support depending on the project."],
  ["Can you deploy the project?", "Yes. Deployment support can include hosting setup, environment variables, domains, production checks, and handoff notes."],
  ["Can you build mobile apps?", "Yes. CodeVault can build mobile apps using React Native, especially for MVPs, internal tools, and product ideas that need both iOS and Android coverage."],
  ["Can you add AI features?", "Yes, when AI actually helps the product. This can include AI writing, summarization, automation, classification, assistants, or workflow acceleration."],
  ["What do you need from me to start?", "A clear idea of the problem, target users, deadline, budget range, examples you like, and any existing assets or code."],
  ["Do you offer ongoing support?", "Yes. After launch, CodeVault can continue with fixes, improvements, new features, and product support through a monthly engagement."],
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="shell" data-reveal>
    <SectionLabel label="Questions" />
    <h2>Before we work together.</h2>

    <div class="faq-stack">
      {faqs.map(([question, answer]) => (
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span>{question}</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{answer}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
